# Linker workarounds for two Cortex-A53 errata. 843419: an ADRP in the last
# two instruction slots of a 4K page (offset 0xff8/0xffc), followed shortly
# by a load or store through its result, can compute the address of the
# next page. 835769: a 64-bit multiply-accumulate right after a load can
# produce a wrong result. Both affect r0p4, which is the A64 in the pine64
# and the little cores of the RK3399 in the rockpro64. The linker rewrites
# the affected sequences through veneers; without this every arm64 binary
# is correct on paper and occasionally wrong on that silicon. Root-caused
# 2026-09-16 from libLLVM.so crashing at startup, see gentoo-build/ISSUES.md
#
# Applied via package.env rather than make.conf because make.conf is shared
# with amd64, whose ld rejects these options. ${LDFLAGS} keeps the profile
# defaults. Packages that link through rustc get it through cc as well
LDFLAGS="${LDFLAGS} -Wl,--fix-cortex-a53-843419 -Wl,--fix-cortex-a53-835769"
